# Docs Terminology and Source Guardrails

This rule provides the terminology reference table and protobuf-leakage guardrail specific to planton.ai/docs content. The complete source verification discipline, three-tier source truth model, and collaboration calibration live in the planton monorepo's documentation rules and are loaded via `@update-planton-ai-docs`.

## Terminology Reference

Use user-facing terms consistently across all documentation. These terms come from what users see in the CLI, web console, and YAML configurations.

| Use This | Not This | Notes |
|----------|----------|-------|
| Infra Component | resource, component (alone) | One deployed instance of a catalog kind in one environment |
| catalog kind | component (for a type), resource type | A type the Infra Catalog offers (AwsS3Bucket); users browse the catalog of kinds |
| Infra Stack | project, deployment | One Infra Chart installed into one environment |
| Infra Job | run, deploy job | The IaC work for one Infra Component |
| provider resource | Infra Component (for what lives in the cloud account) | What a module creates in the cloud account; one Infra Component creates several |
| connection | credential | Except when describing the credential object itself |
| Secrets Manager | Config Manager | User-facing product name |
| Infrastructure (section) | Infra Hub | Section names use user-oriented vocabulary |
| CI/CD (section) | Service Hub | Section names use user-oriented vocabulary |
| Connections (section) | Connect | Matches the web console sidebar label |
| Operations (section) | Cloud Ops | Section names use user-oriented vocabulary |

## Protobuf Leakage Guardrail

Internal identifiers do not belong in user-facing documentation prose unless the user directly writes or reads them.

**Never use in prose:**
- Message type names: `InfraComponentSpec`, `ServicePipelineConfiguration`, `InfraChartParam`
- Field names in running text (acceptable inside YAML code blocks where users type them)
- Enum value names: `DEPLOYMENT_TARGET_KUBERNETES`, `BUILD_METHOD_BUILDPACKS`
- RPC method names: `CreateInfraComponent`, `GetService`, `ListPipelines`

**Acceptable:**
- `apiVersion` and `kind` in YAML manifests users author
- CLI flag names users type (`--env`, `--org`)
- Values that appear in CLI output users read
- YAML field names inside code blocks

Translate internal identifiers into plain language: "deployment target" not `DeploymentTarget`, "Infra Component" not `InfraComponent`.

